dication brief binds its claim and context\""," module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/adjudicate_brief.py\""," code_symbol = \"done_when_values/_subject_claim/_spec_context\"","-detail = \"The done-when class accepts exactly one work item in Adjudicates, reads its claim at the lane integration base while active or at the commit that added the active copy after closure, refuses an unreadable claim, missing Context, or unchanged checklist, and renders both item lists, their changes, the LLR-307 digest, and the spec Context clipped at CANDIDATE_CLIP (120 lines), with any cut stated. Its verdict grammar requires exactly one complete DONE-WHEN line with one of CLARITY, BLESSED or SUCCESSOR and both changes and digest fields. The class is routed and retainable through BRIEF_PROMPTS.\"","+detail = \"The done-when class accepts exactly one work item in Adjudicates, reads its claim at the lane integration base while active or at the commit that added the active copy after closure, refuses an unreadable claim, missing Context, or unchanged checklist, and renders both item lists, their changes, the LLR-307 digest, and the spec Context clipped at CANDIDATE_CLIP (120 lines), with any cut stated. Its verdict grammar reads each physical line separately and requires exactly one complete DONE-WHEN line with one of CLARITY, BLESSED or SUCCESSOR and both changes and digest fields; a split or bare line invalidates it. The class is routed and retainable through BRIEF_PROMPTS.\""," rationale = \"A Done-when verdict must show and bind the exact text the holds evaluate. The brief supplies the claim and bounded purpose context a judge needs to distinguish a clarification from a moved scope.\""," test_refs = \"TC-327\""," status = \"Approved\""]},{"oldStart":3280,"oldLines":8,"newStart":3280,"newLines":8,"lines":[" sr_refs = [\"SR-232\"]"," title = \"Combined sitting composes and validates kind-scoped adjudications\""," module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/adjudicate_brief.py;project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/sitting.py;project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/verdict.py;project-trajectory/scripts/session_service.py;project-trajectory/scripts/coordinator_adjudicate.py\"","-code_symbol = \"requested_kinds/_sitting_scopes/combined_values;scopes/sections/own_section/brief_scope/GRAMMAR/DONE_WHEN_OUTCOMES/line_refusal/named_kinds/sitting_refusal/parse/requested_path/render_requested/read_requested/REQUESTED_SUFFIX/OUTCOMES/write_binding/accepted/accepted_part/accepted_at/judged_rows/_named_line/unaccepted_refusal/REVIEWS/branch_verdicts/uncovered_refusal;row_rulings/ROW_RULINGS;call_succeeded;requested_for/bind_pending/bound_kinds/bind_requested;record_outcome\"","-detail = \"A combined class accepts only amendment:<id>, first-approval:<id> and done-when:<id> Adjudicates tokens; it composes each named class through compose with that section's verdict path in fixed amendment, first-approval, done-when order, and refuses whole if any section cannot compose. One parser reads a verdict into its kind lines: a combined sitting names exactly the kinds bound at reservation in <verdict>.requested, has exactly one kind-form lower-case section per bound kind and none other, and has exactly one complete own-kind machine line in each section; a single-kind verdict has no kind-form section and exactly one complete machine line. One binding records pending before either route calls: the coordinator entry point binds the request exclusively at reservation, and the loop binds its composed request at composition; write_binding is its one writer and record_outcome its one route recorder and commit path, returning its `(outcome, why)` decision and recording accepted only when call_succeeded has derived exit 0, no timeout and no reported error result, and validation passes. call_succeeded is derived once and shared by both routes; a failed call is recorded failed without its verdict being read, and the loop consumes that same why as its completion obligation. The coordinator validates its pending binding before recording its outcome, while the loop records against the kinds read back from its bound request; later consumers use the accepted-verdict reader, which returns only an accepted, bound, valid verdict and each part's row rulings. Every row an adjudication merge act flips needs an APPROVE ruling in an accepted first-approval part, and every row it re-attests needs a MEANING or CLARITY ruling in an accepted amendment part among the branch's own bindings, whether or not the act names a verdict; an accepted verdict over other rows authorizes nothing, and a named verdict must judge each row its act re-attests. Failed, pending, unbound or other-class verdicts cover nothing. Token and section parsing are shared by composition, validation, act scopes and merge-time minting; the class is routed and retainable through BRIEF_PROMPTS.\"","+code_symbol = \"requested_kinds/_sitting_scopes/combined_values;scopes/sections/own_section/brief_scope/GRAMMAR/DONE_WHEN_OUTCOMES/line_refusal/_keyword_lines/_machine_line/_incomplete/_keyword_count_refusal/named_kinds/sitting_refusal/parse/requested_path/render_requested/read_requested/REQUESTED_SUFFIX/OUTCOMES/write_binding/accepted/accepted_part/accepted_at/judged_rows/_named_line/unaccepted_refusal/REVIEWS/branch_verdicts/uncovered_refusal;row_rulings/ROW_RULINGS;call_succeeded;requested_for/bind_pending/bound_kinds/bind_requested;record_outcome\"","+detail = \"A combined class accepts only amendment:<id>, first-approval:<id> and done-when:<id> Adjudicates tokens; it composes each named class through compose with that section's verdict path in fixed amendment, first-approval, done-when order, and refuses whole if any section cannot compose. One parser reads machine lines one physical line at a time: every line whose first token is a machine keyword counts, complete or not, so a bare, split, bad-label or field-missing line invalidates. A combined sitting names exactly the kinds bound at reservation in <verdict>.requested, has exactly one kind-form lower-case section per bound kind and none other, and has across the whole file exactly one complete line per bound kind and one SITTING line, and no line for another kind; a single-kind verdict has no kind-form section and exactly one complete line for its kind. One binding records pending before either route calls: the coordinator entry point binds the request exclusively at reservation, and the loop binds its composed request at composition; write_binding is its one writer and record_outcome its one route recorder and commit path, returning its `(outcome, why)` decision and recording accepted only when call_succeeded has derived exit 0, no timeout and no reported error result, and validation passes. call_succeeded is derived once and shared by both routes; a failed call is recorded failed without its verdict being read, and the loop consumes that same why as its completion obligation. The coordinator validates its pending binding before recording its outcome, while the loop records against the kinds read back from its bound request; later consumers use the accepted-verdict reader, which returns only an accepted, bound, valid verdict and each part's row rulings. Every row an adjudication merge act flips needs an APPROVE ruling in an accepted first-approval part, and every row it re-attests needs a MEANING or CLARITY ruling in an accepted amendment part among the branch's own bindings, whether or not the act names a verdict; an accepted verdict over other rows authorizes nothing, and a named verdict must judge each row its act re-attests. Failed, pending, unbound or other-class verdicts cover nothing. Token and section parsing are shared by composition, validation, act scopes and merge-time minting; the class is routed and retainable through BRIEF_PROMPTS.\""," rationale = \"A shared checkpoint reduces adjudication launches only if no constituent judgement loses its scope or grammar. One parser prevents composition, validation and later acts from interpreting the same sitting differently.\""," test_refs = \"TC-327\""," status = \"Approved\""]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-841\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\README.md","C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-841\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\acts.toml","C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-841\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\requirements\\low-level-requirements.toml"]}}}
