{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfoYHSa11b5F7r1t5W3BH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Verdict: MEANING, rows=2.** It's committed as `06268bea` with the `WI: WI-841` trailer, in `docs/reviews/wi-841-done-when-blessed-in-lane/019-ADJUDICATE-2874ff0.md`.\n\n- **LLR-308 Detail:** the old text only required exactly one complete `DONE-WHEN` line. The new text reads each physical line on its own and rejects the verdict if it has a split or bare `DONE-WHEN` line. A parser that ignored a stray bare line met the old text but fails the new one.\n- **LLR-310 Detail:** machine lines used to be counted section by section, and only complete ones counted. Now they are counted across the whole file, and incomplete ones count too. The verdict must also have exactly one `SITTING` line and no line belonging to another kind, so some verdicts that were valid before are now refused.\n\n**Re-attestation:** the LLR rung is released, so the blessing was mine to give, and I would bless both new texts. The code in `kitlib.sitting` matches them:\n- `_keyword_lines` reads strictly one physical line at a time and keeps bare lines.\n- `_machine_lines` and `_incomplete` reject bare, wrongly labelled or incomplete lines.\n- `_keyword_count_refusal` counts keyword lines over the whole file: one per requested kind, one `SITTING`, and none for any other kind.\n- The `DONE-WHEN` check goes through the same parser.\n\nI didn't run the test suite; I only checked that the code matches the text.\n\nI ran `intake.py snapshot --reattests LLR-308,LLR-310` and committed it separately as `aaee8fbc` (act seq 58). Only the LLR registry was copied, and only those two rows changed. No row's Status changed, no registry cell was edited, and nothing needed a Dispositions entry.\n\nThe same amending commit (`2874ff0a`) also changed `interfaces.toml` and `test-cases.toml`. Those cells weren't put to me, so I left them for another sitting. As before, I left `019-ADJUDICATE-2874ff0.md.requested` uncommitted for the coordinator."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":621,"cache_read_input_tokens":98539,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":621},"output_tokens":724,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6a1938af-a9d5-4d0e-b193-f296d743fff7","uuid":"79f185d3-244d-4c2f-8814-853d620736b7","timestamp":"2026-10-07T20:53:05.752Z","request_id":"req_011CfoYHSFeCPiepdk2eys67"}
